### Explanation

- `FAudioCapture::Init()` attempts to initialize the audio capture interface.
- `FAudioCapture::Start()` takes a lambda (or any delegate matching the expected signature) that receives raw PCM data buffers.
- The callback receives pointers to raw float audio samples, number of samples, channels, sample rate, and stream time.
- The callback is called from an audio thread, so heavy processing should be deferred to the game thread using `AsyncTask`.
- When your game mode ends or is destroyed, be sure to stop and reset the capture object.

