4. Explanation

• The form is divided into several divs—each representing a step. Only one step (div) is “active” at a time. In the code above, for example, #step1 is active at first (all inputs in steps #step2 and #step3 are disabled).

• Each step shows a label, an input field, and a help message (you can style or even use tooltips/popovers with Bootstrap or other libraries).

• The “Next” button (a nonform button) uses JavaScript to validate (a basic nonempty check in the sample) and then disables the current field, removes the current styling, enables the next step’s input and adds the “current-field” style to it. This effectively “guides” the user one field at a time.

• In the last step (#step4) you can display a review message and provide a submit button to send the complete form to the server.

• You can extend the code with additional client-side validations, animations, modal popups for help text, or even use a library like Intro.js for step-by-step guidance.

──────────────────────────────
5. Running the Solution

• Launch your ASP.NET Core application and navigate to the /Registration URL.  
• The user sees only the “Full Name” field highlighted and enabled.  
• Once the field is filled and “Next” is clicked, the form disables that field and moves on to “Email,” highlighting it and showing the context–sensitive help message.  
• Continue until the user reaches the final step and clicks the submit button, which posts the data to the server.

──────────────────────────────
Conclusion

This example shows a simple guided process framework for user registration in ASP.NET Core using a single page. By controlling which input is enabled and highlighting the current field along with context–sensitive help text, you can create a smooth “wizard–like” experience without multiple pages. You can enhance this further by adding better validations (server-side and client-side), advanced animations, and responsive design improvements.

Feel free to adapt or extend this basic approach to suit more complex guided processes.

